    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kootu"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " ",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "kootu",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "kootu"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is bound together by a freshly ground "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "coconut paste",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "coconut-paste"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " stirred in at the end, and finished with a tadka using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "urad dal",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "urad-dal"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " for nuttiness. Any firm vegetable works here: green beans, cabbage, raw plantain, or yam are all traditional choices."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The final consistency should be thick and cohesive, not runny. If using watery vegetables like courgette, cook them down well before adding the coconut paste."
          }
        ]
      },
